---
import PracticeAreaLayout from '../../layouts/PracticeAreaLayout.astro';
---

<PracticeAreaLayout
  title="Protection From Abuse Orders | Maine Volunteer Lawyers Project"
  description="VLP provides free legal assistance with Protection From Abuse (PFA) orders in Maine. Learn about our walk-in PFA clinics in Portland, Biddeford, and Lewiston."
  heading="Protection From Abuse Orders"
  intro="Free legal assistance with Protection From Abuse (PFA) orders. VLP volunteer attorneys provide walk-in representation at district courts across Maine."
  ctaHeading="Need help with a Protection From Abuse order?"
  ctaText="PFA clinic services are walk-in and day-of. Go to your scheduled court hearing and look for the VLP representative at the courthouse."
  ctaIntakeButton={false}
>

  <div slot="body">

    <h2>About Protection From Abuse Orders</h2>
    <p>
      A Protection from Abuse Order is a civil court order that prohibits
      or restricts one person's ability to contact another. An order may
      include contact restrictions, a temporary parenting plan, custody
      arrangements, living arrangements, and child support. The order can
      be in effect for up to 2 years.
    </p>
    <p>
      A Protection from Abuse Order does not replace a divorce or parental
      rights and responsibilities order. You will likely need to file a
      separate case in family court before the PFA expires.
    </p>

    <h3>Who Can File?</h3>
    <p>Regardless of age, you can file against:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Family or household members, or current or former dating partners who have abused you</li>
      <li>Anyone who has stalked you, sexually assaulted you, used or threatened to use intimate images against you, or involved you in sex trafficking</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you are 60 or older, or are a dependent or incapacitated adult, you
      may also file against extended family members or unpaid caregivers. If
      you are a minor, your parent or guardian can file on your behalf.
    </p>

    <h3>Legal Definition of Abuse</h3>
    <p>To qualify for a Protection From Abuse order, the actions must meet specific legal criteria, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Causing or attempting to cause physical injury or offensive physical contact, including sexual assault</li>
      <li>Placing someone in fear through threatening, harassing, or tormenting behavior</li>
      <li>Compelling someone by force, threat, or intimidation</li>
      <li>Knowingly restricting someone's movement without their consent</li>
      <li>Threatening to commit violent crimes</li>
      <li>Repeatedly following or monitoring someone</li>
      <li>Stalking</li>
      <li>Sexual assault</li>
      <li>Sharing private explicit images without consent</li>
      <li>Sex trafficking or aggravated sex trafficking</li>
      <li>Sexually exploiting minors</li>
      <li>Sharing explicit images of minors under 16</li>
      <li>Harassing minors via phone or electronic devices</li>
      <li>Economic abuse (for vulnerable adults)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Court Resources</h3>
    <p>
      The Maine Judicial Branch offers a
      <a href="https://www.courts.maine.gov/help/guides/pa-ph-guide.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">guide to Protection From Abuse and Protection From Harassment orders (PDF)</a>
      and
      <a href="https://www.courts.maine.gov/forms/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">court forms</a>.
      Domestic violence advocates can assist with court navigation, filing, safety planning,
      and general information.
    </p>

    <h2>About This Clinic</h2>

    <div class="notice-box">
      <p>
        <strong>These clinics are walk-in/day-of services only.</strong> If your
        case is continued to another date, an attorney may not be available to
        help you. VLP does not accept direct requests for PFA assistance, please
        see the VLP representative at court on your hearing date. Services are
        free with income-based eligibility.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3>Portland PFA Clinic</h3>
    <p>
      VLP volunteer attorneys provide day-of representation to qualifying
      survivors with cases in Portland District Court who are referred
      directly by <a href="https://www.throughthesedoors.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Through These Doors</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Biddeford PFA Clinic</h3>
    <p>
      VLP volunteer attorneys provide day-of representation to qualifying
      individuals who are the plaintiff in a case where the defendant is
      represented by an attorney, or who are referred by <a href="https://www.caring-unlimited.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Caring Unlimited</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Lewiston PFA Clinic</h3>
    <p>
      VLP volunteer attorneys provide day-of representation to qualifying
      individuals with cases in Lewiston District Court where the other
      party is represented by an attorney or student attorney.
    </p>

    <h3>Statewide Consultation Clinic</h3>
    <p>
      VLP volunteer attorneys provide phone consultations to survivors
      referred by a domestic violence resource center. Attorneys can provide
      legal advice and guidance regarding your upcoming PFA hearing but
      cannot represent you at the hearing.
    </p>

    <h2>Additional Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.ptla.org/free-tags/pfa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pine Tree Legal Assistance</a>  -  PFA resources</li>
      <li><a href="https://mainelse.org/handbook/elder-abuse" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Legal Services for Maine Elders</a>  -  Elder Abuse</li>
      <li><a href="https://maine.freelegalanswers.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Free Legal Answers Maine</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://ircofmaine.org/gender-based-violence-program/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Immigrant Resource Center of Maine</a>  -  Gender-Based Violence Program</li>
      <li><a href="https://mainebar.community.lawyer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maine Lawyer Referral Service</a></li>
    </ul>

  </div>

  <div slot="sidebar">

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--danger">
      <h3>In Immediate Danger?</h3>
      <p><strong>Call 9-1-1</strong></p>
      <p>DV statewide helpline: <a href="tel:8668344357">866-834-HELP</a><br/>Deaf or hard of hearing: <a href="tel:8004371220">800-437-1220</a></p>
      <p>Sexual assault helpline: <a href="tel:8008717741">800-871-7741</a></p>
      <p><a href="https://mcedv.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find your local DV resource center →</a></p>
      <p><a href="https://mecasa.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sexual assault support (MECASA) →</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>How to Access PFA Clinics</h3>
      <p>
        PFA clinics are walk-in, day-of services. There is no advance intake
        form  -  go to your scheduled court date and look for the VLP
        representative at the courthouse.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Clinic Locations</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Portland District Court (referred by Through These Doors)</li>
        <li>Biddeford District Court (referred by Caring Unlimited, or opposing party has attorney)</li>
        <li>Lewiston District Court (opposing party has attorney)</li>
        <li>Statewide phone consultation (referred by DVRC)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Eligibility</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Maine legal matter or Maine court</li>
        <li>Income-based eligibility applies</li>
        <li>Walk-in/day-of only  -  no direct intake requests</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>

</PracticeAreaLayout>
